{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moses shall cast it heavenward.</b> Know that each and every plague among the ten plagues embraces many miracles. Here Scripture mentions 'the full of both your hands' and then says 'and Moses shall cast them' — this tells that the full of both hands, Moses held in one handful, and therefore it says 'and they shall cast' (וזרקו, plural), for a thing cast with force can only be in one hand. And there is yet another miracle: all the land of Egypt was filled with dust from that small quantity of soot — this is what it says: 'and it shall become dust upon all the land of Egypt.' And a third miracle is the plague itself: that that soot became a flying eruption of boils upon man and upon beast."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:11.024171262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}